                                        "entry_id": "036b3d55-dfdb-3883-b3bb-d6448bd797b7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state or quality of being deceitful; duplicity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80a398ef-6d2d-431e-afa8-18795d98001f",
                                                "sense_id": "691a5eb6-844d-3c17-94af-64f87e7afe4e",
                                                "text": "'This is the hend, is it, of all my bearing with her deceitfulness, her lowness, her falseness, her laying herself out to catch the admiration of vulgar minds . . .'"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "703767d1-cf06-4f62-a169-ae092b8454a3",
                                                "sense_id": "691a5eb6-844d-3c17-94af-64f87e7afe4e",
                                                "text": "O full off all sutelte and disseytfulnes the chylde off the devyll, and the enemye of all righteousnes thou ceasest not to pervert the strayght wayes off the lorde."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be38f134-9695-4312-977c-13814332c5cd",
                                                "sense_id": "691a5eb6-844d-3c17-94af-64f87e7afe4e",
                                                "text": "1903, Andy Adams, The Log of a Cowboy: A Narrative of the Old Trail Days, ch. 20 \"A Moonlight Drive\",\nThe lanterns both rear and forward being always in sight, I was as much at sea as any one as to the length of the herd, knowing the deceitfulness of distance of campfires and other lights by night."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
